# Architecture & lineage

Full narrative: [ARCHITECTURE.md](../../ARCHITECTURE.md).

## Active vs historic

This repo is the active toolchain. The parent project’s `archive/` (C sidreloc, ca65 SIDPLAY, old discs) is **not in this tree**.

| Active (this repo) | Historic (parent `archive/`, not present here) |
|--------------------|------------------------------------------------|
| JS sidreloc + ripsid + hash patches | C sidreloc/ripsid, `patch_c64_hw.py`, shell convert |
| BeebAsm `src.player` (source of truth) | ca65 SIDPLAY under `archive/tools/SIDPlayer/` |
| In-memory DFS pack + jsbeeb preview | Dom’s `dfs-0.4`, b-em / py65 host checks |
| In-tree create/player goldens | `archive/output/` older reference discs |

## Pipeline (conceptual)

```text
.sid → [pre-patch] → relocate → [post-patch] → rip → .bbcsid
                                                    ↓
                              pack-ssd (+ sidpl.o) → .ssd → jsbeeb preview
```

## Origins worth remembering

- **SIDPlayer** (Dominic Beesley / Stardot): menu + ripsid + sidreloc workflow this tree ports.
- **sidreloc** (Linus Akesson): JS port in `src.create/src/lib/sidreloc/`.
- **SIDPLAY**: BeebAsm port of ca65 player in `src.player` (not “JS port”).
- **jsbeeb** (Matt Godbolt): headless/browser preview; FastSID via vendored jsSID.
- CLI takes explicit `.sid` paths. Sample library: `sids/` (parent repo called this `input/`). Test fixtures: `src.create/test/golden/`.

Prefer extending this tree over resurrecting parent-repo archive scripts unless the user asks for that parity.

Decision-level “why” from the parent-project birth lives in `.tmp/conversations/` (see historic-conversations rule).
